menu "Sprout feature modules"

config FEATURE_LED_INDICATOR
    bool "Enable status LED indicator"
    default y
    help
        Drive one status LED from LEDC PWM and map device states to bounded
        blink, solid, and breathing patterns. The module keeps the output off
        when the GPIO or LEDC peripheral is unavailable.

config LED_INDICATOR_GPIO
    int "Status LED GPIO number"
    depends on FEATURE_LED_INDICATOR
    range 0 48
    default 38
    help
        Board-profile default is GPIO 38. Change it to the output pin used by
        the product carrier board; the module reports a failure instead of
        driving an invalid pin.

config LED_INDICATOR_ACTIVE_LOW
    bool "Status LED is active low"
    depends on FEATURE_LED_INDICATOR
    default n
    help
        Disabled by default because the current repository has no board
        definition proving an active-low LED. Enable it when the board grounds
        the LED cathode through the GPIO.

config LED_INDICATOR_PWM_FREQUENCY_HZ
    int "LED PWM frequency in Hz"
    depends on FEATURE_LED_INDICATOR
    range 100 5000
    default 1000
    help
        PWM frequencies above the visible flicker range keep brightness
        changes visually smooth.

config LED_INDICATOR_BRIGHTNESS_PERCENT
    int "LED brightness percent"
    depends on FEATURE_LED_INDICATOR
    range 1 100
    default 50
    help
        Relative duty applied to solid, blink, and breathing patterns.

config LED_INDICATOR_TASK_STACK_SIZE
    int "Indicator task stack size in bytes"
    depends on FEATURE_LED_INDICATOR
    range 2048 8192
    default 3072

config LED_INDICATOR_TASK_PRIORITY
    int "Indicator task priority"
    depends on FEATURE_LED_INDICATOR
    range 1 12
    default 2
    help
        The indicator only updates PWM and must remain below audio, network,
        and watchdog work.

config LED_INDICATOR_POLL_INTERVAL_MS
    int "Pattern transition poll interval in milliseconds"
    depends on FEATURE_LED_INDICATOR
    range 5 1000
    default 20
    help
        Bounds how long the task waits before applying a new state. The task
        blocks on a semaphore or this timeout and never busy-spins.

endmenu
